From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:49:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A networked output offers the 3D formats and the eye swap of a monitor

An output made for a device on the network without split eyes gets the VirtualStereo and StereoSwapEyes
capabilities, so Display Settings offers its Anaglyph and Other stereo formats switches and its eye swap.
VirtualOutput and DrmVirtualOutput make the format twins of its 2D mode from those switches (side by side
half and top and bottom, the modern and CRT anaglyph twins), and a twin the switches no longer offer goes
with the screen back in 2D. It arrives in 2D at the device mode; the configuration store gives back the
format, switches and swap the person chose for that device (its persistent name is the output's
identity) when the saved mode is a twin of the device's current mode. Split-eye outputs are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
diff --git a/src/backends/drm/drm_virtual_output.cpp b/src/backends/drm/drm_virtual_output.cpp
index 97276b8..a02146a 100644
--- a/src/backends/drm/drm_virtual_output.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/drm/drm_virtual_output.cpp
@@ -144,6 +144,15 @@ void DrmVirtualOutput::applyChanges(const OutputConfiguration &config)
         next.modes = newModes;
     }
 
+    if (offersNetworkFormats()) {
+        // a network screen makes the format twins of its 2D mode from the person's switches, as a monitor does;
+        // a twin the switches no longer offer goes, and the screen is back in 2D
+        next.modes = withNetworkFormatModes(next.modes, next.anaglyph, next.otherStereoFormats);
+        if (next.currentMode && !next.modes.contains(next.currentMode)) {
+            next.currentMode = nullptr;
+        }
+    }
+
     next.desiredMode = props->desiredMode.value_or(m_state.desiredMode);
     if (props->currentMode) {
         next.currentMode = props->currentMode->match(next.modes);
